---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SEO from '../components/SEO.astro';
import AdSense from '../components/AdSense.astro';
import FuelConverter from '../components/tools/FuelConverter';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <SEO slot="head" title="Fuel Economy Converter" description="Convert between MPG, km/L, and L/100km fuel economy units." />
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do I convert MPG to L/100km?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Divide 235.215 by the MPG value. For example, 30 MPG ≈ 7.84 L/100km.\"}}]}"} />

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-primary-600">Home</a> <span class="mx-2">›</span> <span class="text-gray-900">Fuel Economy Converter</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Fuel Economy Converter</h1>

    <FuelConverter client:load />

    <AdSense slot="middle" />

    <div class="mt-12 prose prose-gray max-w-none">
      <h2>How to Convert Fuel Economy</h2><p>Fuel economy is measured differently around the world: the US uses miles per gallon (MPG), while most other countries use liters per 100 kilometers (L/100km) or kilometers per liter (km/L).</p><h3>Important Note</h3><p>MPG and L/100km have an inverse relationship: higher MPG means lower L/100km (better fuel economy). This makes direct comparison tricky without a converter.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="border-b border-gray-100 pb-4 last:border-0">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How do I convert MPG to L/100km?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-600">Divide 235.215 by the MPG value. For example, 30 MPG ≈ 7.84 L/100km.</p>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <AdSense slot="bottom" />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
